window.DOCS["6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172"]={"id":"6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172","summary":{"title_zh":"議程項目 17 (c) 第二工作小組非正式文本（第 4 版）：保護區工作計畫的策略審查與更新","what":"這是第二工作小組的非正式文本（第 4 版），內容為更新保護區工作計畫，使其與綱要目標 3 一致，並將計畫名稱擴大為「保護區及保育共生地」。文件中仍有多項內容（包括是否新增生態連結性為第五個要素）尚未達成共識。","points":["決定更新保護區工作計畫，使其與綱要目標 3 一致，並將計畫名稱改為包含「保育共生地」（承認原住民族與傳統領地「如適用」的措辭尚未達成共識）。","鼓勵締約方與其他政府，依國情、法律與優先事項，在制定與執行行動時納入更新後的計畫，特別是目標 3。","邀請各相關秘書處、國際組織、聯合國機構、原住民族與地方社區、私部門、學術界、非政府組織、女性與青年等，透過知識交流、科學與技術合作及能力建構支持綱要的執行。","請求執行秘書在資源允許下，支持「目標 3 社群實務」，並促進協調與知識交流（是否彙整各方經驗撰寫綜合報告，尚未達成共識）。","鼓勵締約方執行更新後的計畫時，依綱要 C 節與《生物多樣性公約》第 8(j) 條等規定，確保原住民族與地方社區、女性、女童與青年充分有效參與（以人權為基礎的做法與保護環境人權捍衛者的措辭尚未達成共識）。","[尚未達成共識] 第 11 段擬決定在工作計畫中新增「生態連結性」作為第五個要素；替代版則為邀請締約方在執行中加強生態連結性。"],"open":["第 5 段：主版「邀請締約方動員新的、可預測且充足的資金（包括來自所有來源）」與替代版「鼓勵締約方依公約第 20 條與第 21 條提供財務與技術支持」的選擇（整段方括號）（尚未達成共識）。","第 11 段與替代版 11 alt：是否決定將生態連結性新增為工作計畫的第五個要素，或僅邀請締約方加強生態連結性（尚未達成共識）。","第 10 段與第 12 段：是否於第十八次締約方大會前決定需要額外指引，並以期間工作進一步發展對生態連結性與代表性的理解（尚未達成共識）。","序言與第 2 段：生態代表性與連結性應為「品質要求」還是「基礎條件」，以及名稱與各段中是否承認「原住民族與傳統領地（如適用）」（尚未達成共識）。","第 8 段：是否以「人權為基礎的做法」執行工作計畫，以及是否加入保護環境人權捍衛者的措辭（尚未達成共識）。","第 13(c) 段與替代版 13(c) Alt：綜合報告的投入來源是否包括次國家級政府與地方政府，以及其重點領域（尚未達成共識）。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p001.md","en":[{"t":"Agenda item 17 (c)"},{"t":"Scientific and technical needs to support the implementation"},{"t":"of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework"},{"t":"and matters related to the work programme of the"},{"t":"Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity"},{"t":"and Ecosystem Services: strategic review of and updates to"},{"t":"the programme of work on protected areas"},{"t":"Working Group II"},{"t":"Scientific and technical needs to support the implementation of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework: strategic review of"},{"t":"and update to the programme of work on protected areas"},{"t":"Non-paper – version 4"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties,"},{"t":"Recalling its decisions VII/28 of 20 February 2004, VIII/24 of 31 March 2006, IX/18 of 30 May 2008, X/31 of 29 October 2010, 14/8 of 29 November 2018, 15/4 of 19 December 2022 and 16/12 of 1 November 2024,"},{"t":"Acknowledging that the programme of work on protected areas1 and related decisions of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity2 continue to provide a strategic framework for the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,3 in particular Target 3, while noting that complementary activities are needed to enhance its alignment with the Framework and address identified gaps,"},{"t":"Recognizing that [ecological representativeness and] ecological connectivity [are critical qualitative requirements][is a foundational condition] for achieving ecologically representative, well-connected, effectively conserved and managed, and equitably governed systems[ of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] under Target 3 of the Framework, and contributes to the achievement of other relevant targets and Goal A of the Framework,"},{"t":"[Noting the ongoing preparation by the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services on the methodological assessment of integrated biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning and ecological connectivity, and its potential relevance for the further [development and] implementation of the programme of work,]"},{"t":"1.   Takes note of the forthcoming seventh International Union for Conservation of Nature World Protected and Conserved Areas Congress, organized in Panama by the International Union for Conservation of Nature, the World Commission on Protected Areas and the Ministry of Environment of Panama;"},{"t":"2.    Decides to update the existing programme of work on protected areas in a manner consistent with Target 3 of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, in accordance with national circumstances and legislation and to revise the name of the programme of work on protected areas to the programme of work on protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures[, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable];"},{"t":"3.    [Endorses] the complementary activities for further or improved guidance contained in the annex to the present decision as an update to the programme of work to support the implementation of the Framework, with particular focus on Target 3;"},{"t":"1 Decision VII/28, annex."},{"t":"2 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"3 Decision 15/4, annex."}],"blocks":[{"md":"議程項目 17 (c)\n支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求，以及與生物多樣性及生態系政府間科學－政策平台工作計畫相關事項：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新\n第二工作小組","html":"<p>議程項目 17 (c)<br />\n支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求，以及與生物多樣性及生態系政府間科學－政策平台工作計畫相關事項：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新<br />\n第二工作小組</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新\n非正式文件 – 第 4 版","html":"<p>支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新<br />\n非正式文件 – 第 4 版</p>","en":[5,6,7,8]},{"md":"締約方大會，","html":"<p>締約方大會，</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"**回顧**其 2004 年 2 月 20 日之決議 VII/28、2006 年 3 月 31 日之決議 VIII/24、2008 年 5 月 30 日之決議 IX/18、2010 年 10 月 29 日之決議 X/31、2018 年 11 月 29 日之決議 14/8、2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/4 以及 2024 年 11 月 1 日之決議 16/12，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其 2004 年 2 月 20 日之決議 VII/28、2006 年 3 月 31 日之決議 VIII/24、2008 年 5 月 30 日之決議 IX/18、2010 年 10 月 29 日之決議 X/31、2018 年 11 月 29 日之決議 14/8、2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/4 以及 2024 年 11 月 1 日之決議 16/12，</p>","en":[10,11,12,13]},{"md":"**承認**保護區工作計畫$^1$及《生物多樣性公約》$^2$締約方之相關決議，持續為實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要$^3$（特別是目標 3）提供策略性框架，同時**注意到**需要補充性活動以強化其與綱要的一致性並解決已識別之差距，","html":"<p><strong>承認</strong>保護區工作計畫<sup>1</sup>及《生物多樣性公約》<sup>2</sup>締約方之相關決議，持續為實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>3</sup>（特別是目標 3）提供策略性框架，同時<strong>注意到</strong>需要補充性活動以強化其與綱要的一致性並解決已識別之差距，</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"**認識到**[生態代表性與]生態連結性[是關鍵的品質要求][是基礎條件]，對於在綱要目標 3 下實現具生態代表性、高度連結、有效保育與管理，且治理公平之系統[（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）的保護區與保育共生地]，以及有助於達成綱要其他相關目標與長期目標 A，具有重要意義，","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>[生態代表性與]生態連結性[是關鍵的品質要求][是基礎條件]，對於在綱要目標 3 下實現具生態代表性、高度連結、有效保育與管理，且治理公平之系統[（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）的保護區與保育共生地]，以及有助於達成綱要其他相關目標與長期目標 A，具有重要意義，</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"[**注意到**生物多樣性及生態系政府間科學－政策平台目前正進行整合性生物多樣性友善空間規劃與生態連結性的方法論評估準備工作，及其對於工作計畫進一步[發展與]實施之潛在相關性，]","html":"<p>[<strong>注意到</strong>生物多樣性及生態系政府間科學－政策平台目前正進行整合性生物多樣性友善空間規劃與生態連結性的方法論評估準備工作，及其對於工作計畫進一步[發展與]實施之潛在相關性，]</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"1.  **注意到**即將於巴拿馬舉行之第七屆國際自然保護聯盟世界保護區與保育區大會，該會議由國際自然保護聯盟、世界保護區委員會及巴拿馬環境部共同主辦；","html":"<p>1.  <strong>注意到</strong>即將於巴拿馬舉行之第七屆國際自然保護聯盟世界保護區與保育區大會，該會議由國際自然保護聯盟、世界保護區委員會及巴拿馬環境部共同主辦；</p>","en":[17]},{"md":"2.  **決定**以符合昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要目標 3 之方式，並根據國家情況與立法，更新現行之保護區工作計畫，並將保護區工作計畫之名稱修訂為「保護區與保育共生地工作計畫」[（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）]；","html":"<p>2.  <strong>決定</strong>以符合昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要目標 3 之方式，並根據國家情況與立法，更新現行之保護區工作計畫，並將保護區工作計畫之名稱修訂為「保護區與保育共生地工作計畫」[（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）]；</p>","en":[18]},{"md":"3.  [**贊同**]本決議附件中所載之旨在提供進一步或改進指引的補充性活動，作為工作計畫之更新，以支持綱要之實施，並特別關注目標 3；","html":"<p>3.  [<strong>贊同</strong>]本決議附件中所載之旨在提供進一步或改進指引的補充性活動，作為工作計畫之更新，以支持綱要之實施，並特別關注目標 3；</p>","en":[19]},{"md":"---\n$^1$ 決議 VII/28，附件。\n$^2$ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^3$ 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>1</sup> 決議 VII/28，附件。<br />\n<sup>2</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>3</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>","en":[20,21,22]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p002.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"4.    Encourages Parties and other Governments to integrate the updated programme of work in the development and implementation of actions to meet the relevant targets of the Framework, in particular Target 3, subject to national circumstances, legislation and priorities;"},{"t":"[5. Invites Parties, and invites other governments and relevant stakeholders, organizations and financial institutions, to mobilize in accordance with Article 20 and decision 16/34 of the Convention and consistent with target 19 of the Framework new additional, predictable, adequate, timely and accessible financial resources from all sources to collectively scale up investments for the effective implementation of the updated programme of work, in particular for developing countries, including small island developing states;]"},{"t":"[5. Alt      Encourages parties, in accordance with articles 20 and 21 of the Convention on","tb":1},{"t":"biological diversity and invites other governments, subnational and local governments and relevant organizations and actors in a position to do so, to provide financial and technical support, to support the implementation of the updated programme of work, taking into consideration the specific situations of developing country parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing states, in accordance with paragraph 6 of article 20 of the Convention;]"},{"t":"6.     Recognizes the importance of mobilizing predictable, adequate and sustainable means of implementation, including through financial resources, technical and scientific cooperation and capacity-building, to ensure the effective implementation of the updated programme of work;"},{"t":"7.     Invites the secretariats of relevant biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements, international organizations and United Nations entities, including the Global Partnership on Ecological Connectivity, indigenous peoples and local communities, including the private sector, academia, non-governmental organizations, women, youth and other relevant stakeholders, to contribute to the implementation of the Framework by supporting knowledge exchange, technical and scientific cooperation, capacity-building and development, and coordinated action in the implementation of the updated programme of work;"},{"t":"8.    Encourages Parties [to apply a human rights-based approach in the implementation of][to implement] the updated programme of work, consistent with section C [and Target 22] of the Framework and Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities, including by ensuring the full, equitable, inclusive and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, [recognizing their own governance systems,] [women, girls and youth, and, as appropriate, the protection of environmental human rights defenders];"},{"t":"9.     Invites Parties to take into consideration findings from relevant assessments of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services when implementing the updated programme of work and to engage in the preparations of the methodological assessment on integrated biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning and ecological connectivity;"},{"t":"[10. Decides to consider at its eighteenth meeting, as appropriate, whether additional guidance is required in relation to strengthening the foundational qualitative conditions for achieving ecologically representative, well-connected, effectively conserved and managed, and equitably governed systems of [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable] in line with Target 3, and to the support of the development of actions to meet the related relevant targets of the Framework, in particular [Targets 1 to 6, 10 and 12], based on recommendations from the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at its meeting held prior to the eighteenth Conference of the Parties, taking into account the relevant Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services assessments and other relevant scientific and technical information, as appropriate, including ecological connectivity and representativity, decision 14/8 annex 1 and other relevant ongoing work in particular under decision 17/xx (outcome of Agenda Item 17d);]"},{"t":"2/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"4.\n**鼓勵**締約方及其他政府，在制定與執行旨在達成綱要相關目標（特別是目標 3）之行動時，應視國家情況、立法與優先事項，納入更新後的工作計畫；","html":"<p>4.<br />\n<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方及其他政府，在制定與執行旨在達成綱要相關目標（特別是目標 3）之行動時，應視國家情況、立法與優先事項，納入更新後的工作計畫；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"[5. **邀請**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府、相關利害關係人、組織與金融機構，根據《公約》第 20 條及決議 16/34，並與綱要目標 19 保持一致，從所有來源動員新的、額外的、可預測、充足、及時且可取得之財務資源，以共同擴大投資，用於有效落實更新後的工作計畫，特別是針對開發中國家，包括小島嶼開發中國家；]","html":"<p>[5. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府、相關利害關係人、組織與金融機構，根據《公約》第 20 條及決議 16/34，並與綱要目標 19 保持一致，從所有來源動員新的、額外的、可預測、充足、及時且可取得之財務資源，以共同擴大投資，用於有效落實更新後的工作計畫，特別是針對開發中國家，包括小島嶼開發中國家；]</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"[5. 替代方案\n**鼓勵**締約方，根據《生物多樣性公約》第 20 條與第 21 條，並**邀請**其他政府、次國家級政府與地方政府，以及有能力之相關組織與行動者，提供財務與技術支援，以支持更新後工作計畫之落實，並應根據《公約》第 20 條第 6 項，考量開發中國家締約方之特殊情況，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家；]","html":"<p>[5. 替代方案<br />\n<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，根據《生物多樣性公約》第 20 條與第 21 條，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府、次國家級政府與地方政府，以及有能力之相關組織與行動者，提供財務與技術支援，以支持更新後工作計畫之落實，並應根據《公約》第 20 條第 6 項，考量開發中國家締約方之特殊情況，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家；]</p>","en":[3,4]},{"md":"6.\n**認識到**動員可預測、充足且永續之實施手段（包括透過財務資源、技術與科學合作以及能力建構）對於確保有效落實更新後工作計畫之重要性；","html":"<p>6.<br />\n<strong>認識到</strong>動員可預測、充足且永續之實施手段（包括透過財務資源、技術與科學合作以及能力建構）對於確保有效落實更新後工作計畫之重要性；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"7.\n**邀請**相關生物多樣性相關公約與其他多邊環境協議之秘書處、國際組織與聯合國實體（包括生態連結全球夥伴關係）、原住民族與地方社區（包括私營部門、學術界、非政府組織、女性、青年）以及其他相關利害關係人，透過支持知識交換、技術與科學合作、能力建構與發展，以及在落實更新後工作計畫中的協調行動，為綱要之落實做出貢獻；","html":"<p>7.<br />\n<strong>邀請</strong>相關生物多樣性相關公約與其他多邊環境協議之秘書處、國際組織與聯合國實體（包括生態連結全球夥伴關係）、原住民族與地方社區（包括私營部門、學術界、非政府組織、女性、青年）以及其他相關利害關係人，透過支持知識交換、技術與科學合作、能力建構與發展，以及在落實更新後工作計畫中的協調行動，為綱要之落實做出貢獻；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"8.\n**鼓勵**締約方[在落實更新後工作計畫時採用以人權為基礎之方法][落實]更新後的工作計畫，並與綱要 C 部分[及目標 22]以及《公約》中與原住民族與地方社區相關之第 8(j) 條及其他條款保持一致，包括確保原住民族與地方社區之充分、公平、包容且有效之參與，[承認其自身之治理體系，][女性、女孩與青年，並在適當時，保護環境人權捍衛者]；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方[在落實更新後工作計畫時採用以人權為基礎之方法][落實]更新後的工作計畫，並與綱要 C 部分[及目標 22]以及《公約》中與原住民族與地方社區相關之第 8(j) 條及其他條款保持一致，包括確保原住民族與地方社區之充分、公平、包容且有效之參與，[承認其自身之治理體系，][女性、女孩與青年，並在適當時，保護環境人權捍衛者]；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"9.\n**邀請**締約方在落實更新後工作計畫時，應考量「生物多樣性與生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台」相關評估之結果，並參與關於整合生物多樣性友善空間規劃與生態連結之方法論評估之準備工作；","html":"<p>9.<br />\n<strong>邀請</strong>締約方在落實更新後工作計畫時，應考量「生物多樣性與生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台」相關評估之結果，並參與關於整合生物多樣性友善空間規劃與生態連結之方法論評估之準備工作；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"[10. **決定**於第十八次會議中，視適當時，根據科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構在其第十八次締約方大會前召開之會議所提出之建議，並考量相關「生物多樣性與生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台」評估及其他相關科學與技術資訊（視適當時，包括生態連結與代表性，決議 14/8 附件 1 以及特別是在決議 17/xx（議程項目 17d 之結果）下之其他相關進行中工作），評估是否需要額外指導，以強化達成符合目標 3 之具生態代表性、良好連結、有效保育與管理，且治理公平之[保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）]之基礎品質條件，以及支持開發旨在達成綱要相關目標（特別是[目標 1 至 6、10 與 12]）之行動；]","html":"<p>[10. <strong>決定</strong>於第十八次會議中，視適當時，根據科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構在其第十八次締約方大會前召開之會議所提出之建議，並考量相關「生物多樣性與生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台」評估及其他相關科學與技術資訊（視適當時，包括生態連結與代表性，決議 14/8 附件 1 以及特別是在決議 17/xx（議程項目 17d 之結果）下之其他相關進行中工作），評估是否需要額外指導，以強化達成符合目標 3 之具生態代表性、良好連結、有效保育與管理，且治理公平之[保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）]之基礎品質條件，以及支持開發旨在達成綱要相關目標（特別是[目標 1 至 6、10 與 12]）之行動；]</p>","en":[9,10]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p003.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"[11. [Decides to establish a fifth programme element][Endorses a cross-cutting complementary activity] on ecological connectivity within the programme of work, as set out in section II of the annex to the present decision, recognizing ecological connectivity as one of several foundational conditions for achieving ecologically representative, well-connected, effectively conserved and managed, and equitably governed systems[ of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], to support the development and implementation of actions to meet the relevant targets of the Framework[, in particular Targets 1 to 6, 9 and 12];]"},{"t":"11 Alt.      Invites Parties to reinforce ecological connectivity in the implementation of the","tb":1},{"t":"updated programme of work, in line with the relevant complementary activities set out in the annex to the present decision and in support of the implementation of the Framework;"},{"t":"[12. Decides to work intersessionally to further develop an understanding [of how][options on how] to strengthen the programme of work in relation to ecological connectivity, [and ecological representativeness] including [consideration of possible additional programme of work updates or elements][through the consideration of a possible fifth element], taking into account inter alia the elements [such as][integrated spatial planning][and cooperation and coordination][contained in section II of the annex], and requests the executive secretary to compile views of the parties for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at its meeting prior to the eighteenth Conference of the Parties]"},{"t":"13. Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources and avoiding duplication with other ongoing initiatives and relevant programmes of work:"},{"t":"(a) To further support the Target 3 Community of Practice as a flexible, inclusive and voluntary platform, with a view to facilitating coordination, knowledge exchange and implementation support, and to invite indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth, relevant organizations and initiatives to participate in the Community;"},{"t":"(b) To collaborate with the regional and subregional technical and scientific cooperation support centres and other relevant partners in order to deliver targeted scientific and technical support to Parties for meeting Target 3 of the Framework, based on the best available information and the best practices identified pursuant to subparagraph (c) (vii) below;"},{"t":"[(c) To compile, with input from Parties, other Governments, [subnational and local governments], relevant organizations and other stakeholders[, within their respective mandates, and recognizing traditional territories, where applicable], a synthesis report on experiences, lessons learned and different approaches, as well as relevant scientific information, including the findings of the assessments of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services that support the achievement of Target 3 of the Framework and the implementation of the programme of work [in a manner consistent with Target 3] [, with particular focus on the following areas:"},{"t":"[(c) Alt.     To compile with input from parties, other governments at all levels, relevant","tb":1},{"t":"organizations, [indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth] and other stakeholders, a synthesis report on experiences, lessons learned and different approaches, as well as relevant scientific information, including the findings of the assessments of the intergovernmental science policy platform on biodiversity and ecosystem services that support the achievement of target 3 of the Framework and the implementation of the programme of work] [with particular focus on the following areas:"},{"t":"(i)    Equitable governance approaches, including the recognition and respect of the rights and contributions of indigenous peoples and local communities and other groups, including through the implementation of relevant targets of the Framework;"},{"t":"3/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper） – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper） – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"[11. [決定建立第五個工作計畫要素][核准工作計畫內的一項跨領域補充活動]關於生態連結性，如本決議附件第二節所述，並承認生態連結性是實現具生態代表性、良好連結、有效保育與管理，以及公平治理之系統[之保護區與保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]的數個基礎條件之一，以支持開發與執行符合綱要相關目標之行動[, 特別是目標 1 至 6、9 與 12]；]","html":"<p>[11. [決定建立第五個工作計畫要素][核准工作計畫內的一項跨領域補充活動]關於生態連結性，如本決議附件第二節所述，並承認生態連結性是實現具生態代表性、良好連結、有效保育與管理，以及公平治理之系統[之保護區與保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]的數個基礎條件之一，以支持開發與執行符合綱要相關目標之行動[, 特別是目標 1 至 6、9 與 12]；]</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"11 替代案\n邀請締約方在執行更新後的工作計畫時強化生態連結性，與本決議附件所述之相關補充活動一致，並支持綱要之實施；","html":"<p>11 替代案<br />\n邀請締約方在執行更新後的工作計畫時強化生態連結性，與本決議附件所述之相關補充活動一致，並支持綱要之實施；</p>","en":[2,3]},{"md":"[12. 決定於會期外進行工作，以進一步深化對[如何][如何之選項]強化與生態連結性相關之工作計畫的理解，[以及生態代表性]，包括[考慮可能對工作計畫進行之額外更新或要素][透過考慮可能之第五個要素]，並在考慮其他要素之際，例如[如][整合性空間規劃][與合作與協調][包含於附件第二節中]，並請求執行秘書彙編締約方之意見，供科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構在其第十八次締約方大會之前的會議上審議]","html":"<p>[12. 決定於會期外進行工作，以進一步深化對[如何][如何之選項]強化與生態連結性相關之工作計畫的理解，[以及生態代表性]，包括[考慮可能對工作計畫進行之額外更新或要素][透過考慮可能之第五個要素]，並在考慮其他要素之際，例如[如][整合性空間規劃][與合作與協調][包含於附件第二節中]，並請求執行秘書彙編締約方之意見，供科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構在其第十八次締約方大會之前的會議上審議]</p>","en":[4,5,6,7]},{"md":"13. 請求執行秘書，在資源可用且避免與其他進行中之倡議及相關工作計畫重複之情況下：\n(a) 進一步支持目標 3 實務社群作為一個彈性、包容且自願性的平台，旨在促進協調、知識交流與執行支持，並邀請原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、相關組織與倡議參與該社群；\n(b) 與區域及次區域技術與科學合作支持中心及其他相關夥伴合作，以便根據最佳可用資訊以及根據下文第 (c) (vii) 小節所識別之最佳實務，為締約方提供有針對性的科學與技術支持，以達成綱要之目標 3；\n[(c) 在締約方、其他政府、[次國家級與地方政府]、相關組織及其他利害關係人之投入下，[在其各自職權範圍內，並在適用時承認傳統領地]，彙編一份關於經驗、經驗教訓與不同方法，以及相關科學資訊的綜合報告，包括政府間科學－政策平台對生物多樣性及生態系服務之評估結果，以支持達成綱要目標 3 及工作計畫之實施[並與目標 3 保持一致] [, 並特別關注以下領域：\n[(c) 替代案\n在締約方、各級其他政府、相關組織、[原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年]及其他利害關係人之投入下，彙編一份關於經驗、經驗教訓與不同方法，以及相關科學資訊的綜合報告，包括政府間科學－政策平台對生物多樣性及生態系服務之評估結果，以支持達成綱要目標 3 及工作計畫之實施] [並特別關注以下領域：\n(i)\n公平治理方法，包括承認並尊重原住民族與地方社區及其他群體之權利與貢獻，包括透過實施綱要之相關目標；","html":"<p>13. 請求執行秘書，在資源可用且避免與其他進行中之倡議及相關工作計畫重複之情況下：<br />\n(a) 進一步支持目標 3 實務社群作為一個彈性、包容且自願性的平台，旨在促進協調、知識交流與執行支持，並邀請原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、相關組織與倡議參與該社群；<br />\n(b) 與區域及次區域技術與科學合作支持中心及其他相關夥伴合作，以便根據最佳可用資訊以及根據下文第 (c) (vii) 小節所識別之最佳實務，為締約方提供有針對性的科學與技術支持，以達成綱要之目標 3；<br />\n[(c) 在締約方、其他政府、[次國家級與地方政府]、相關組織及其他利害關係人之投入下，[在其各自職權範圍內，並在適用時承認傳統領地]，彙編一份關於經驗、經驗教訓與不同方法，以及相關科學資訊的綜合報告，包括政府間科學－政策平台對生物多樣性及生態系服務之評估結果，以支持達成綱要目標 3 及工作計畫之實施[並與目標 3 保持一致] [, 並特別關注以下領域：<br />\n[(c) 替代案<br />\n在締約方、各級其他政府、相關組織、[原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年]及其他利害關係人之投入下，彙編一份關於經驗、經驗教訓與不同方法，以及相關科學資訊的綜合報告，包括政府間科學－政策平台對生物多樣性及生態系服務之評估結果，以支持達成綱要目標 3 及工作計畫之實施] [並特別關注以下領域：<br />\n(i)<br />\n公平治理方法，包括承認並尊重原住民族與地方社區及其他群體之權利與貢獻，包括透過實施綱要之相關目標；</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p004.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"(ii)     Ecological integrity, representativeness, effective conservation, ecosystem restoration and resilience, and ecological connectivity across terrestrial, wetland, inland water, coastal and marine ecosystems, including in the context of climate change;"},{"t":"(iii)    The recognition of indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable [under Target 3 of the Framework], including by applying differentiated approaches for indigenous peoples in voluntary isolation and initial contact[, in line with the principles of no contact, intangibility and precaution], based on the outcomes of Tasks 1.1 and 1.2 of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 2030, as contained in decision 17/xx;"},{"t":"(iv)     Gender equality and gender‑responsive and intergenerational approaches, and the integration of traditional knowledge, in planning, governance and [the] management [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable];"},{"t":"(v)      The integration of [well-connected and equitably governed systems of] [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] into broader landscapes and seascapes [and the ocean], across areas within and beyond national jurisdiction,[ in line with [the mandates of the Agreement under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea on the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction, 4 the International Maritime Organization, the International Seabed Authority, regional fisheries management organizations and other] relevant international organizations,] including through biodiversity‑inclusive and participatory spatial planning;"},{"t":"(vi)     The identification and prioritization of areas of particular importance for biodiversity, ecosystem functions and services, and biocultural diversity, including underrepresented ecosystems and areas supporting ecological networks below ground;"},{"t":"(vii) Planning, governance and [the] effective management [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including the integration of climate change considerations and participatory risk assessment into species and ecosystem conservation, as well as the management of human-wildlife conflict to promote coexistence, as key conditions for achieving management effectiveness, including examples and best practices for other effective area-based conservation measures;"},{"t":"(viii) Ecological networks, conservation mosaics, climate‑informed spatial planning and corridor design, ecological connectivity on varying scales, transboundary conservation and its contribution to peace, and restoration, including in urban and peri-urban contexts;"},{"t":"(ix)     Monitoring and evaluation systems [for protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including through biodiversity monitoring and the use of relevant new technologies, community-based monitoring, the strengthening of national biodiversity databases, among other relevant dimensions, and, where possible, the principles of findability, accessibility, interoperability and reusability (FAIR) and of collective benefit, authority to control, responsibility and ethics (CARE)[, in accordance with national circumstances and legislation];"},{"t":"(x)      Sustainable finance approaches, innovative financial mechanisms, including from public and private sources [and environmental and social safeguards], relevant to the"},{"t":"4 A/CONF.232/2023/4."},{"t":"4/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"(ii)","html":"<p>(ii)</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"跨陸域、濕地、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系之生態完整性、代表性、有效保育、生態系復育與韌性，以及生態連結性，包括在氣候變遷背景下；","html":"<p>跨陸域、濕地、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系之生態完整性、代表性、有效保育、生態系復育與韌性，以及生態連結性，包括在氣候變遷背景下；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"(iii)","html":"<p>(iii)</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"對原住民族與傳統領地的承認（若適用）[於綱要目標 3 之下]，包括對處於自願隔離與初步接觸狀態的原住民族採用差異化方法[, 並符合不接觸、不可侵犯及預防原則]，其基礎應基於關於 2030 年前第 8(j) 條工作計畫之任務 1.1 與 1.2 之成果，以及公約中與原住民族與地方社區相關之其他規定，如決議 17/xx 所載；","html":"<p>對原住民族與傳統領地的承認（若適用）[於綱要目標 3 之下]，包括對處於自願隔離與初步接觸狀態的原住民族採用差異化方法[, 並符合不接觸、不可侵犯及預防原則]，其基礎應基於關於 2030 年前第 8(j) 條工作計畫之任務 1.1 與 1.2 之成果，以及公約中與原住民族與地方社區相關之其他規定，如決議 17/xx 所載；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(iv)","html":"<p>(iv)</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"在規劃、治理與 [該] 管理 [保護區及保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（若適用）]，納入性別平等、具性別回應性與跨世代之方法，以及傳統知識之整合；","html":"<p>在規劃、治理與 [該] 管理 [保護區及保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（若適用）]，納入性別平等、具性別回應性與跨世代之方法，以及傳統知識之整合；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"(v)","html":"<p>(v)</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"將 [具良好連結性且治理公平之] [保護區及保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（若適用）] 整合至更廣泛的景觀與海景 [及海洋] 中，範圍涵蓋國家管轄範圍內與範圍外，[並符合 [聯合國海洋法公約下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育及永續利用協定之授權、國際海事組織、國際海底管理局、區域漁業管理組織及其他] 相關國際組織之授權，] 包括透過具生物多樣性包容性且具參與性的空間規劃；","html":"<p>將 [具良好連結性且治理公平之] [保護區及保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（若適用）] 整合至更廣泛的景觀與海景 [及海洋] 中，範圍涵蓋國家管轄範圍內與範圍外，[並符合 [聯合國海洋法公約下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育及永續利用協定之授權、國際海事組織、國際海底管理局、區域漁業管理組織及其他] 相關國際組織之授權，] 包括透過具生物多樣性包容性且具參與性的空間規劃；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(vi)","html":"<p>(vi)</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"識別並優先考慮對生物多樣性、生態系功能與服務，以及生物文化多樣性具有特別重要性之區域，包括代表性不足之生態系，以及支持地下生態網絡之區域；","html":"<p>識別並優先考慮對生物多樣性、生態系功能與服務，以及生物文化多樣性具有特別重要性之區域，包括代表性不足之生態系，以及支持地下生態網絡之區域；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(vii)","html":"<p>(vii)</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"保護區及保育共生地之規劃、治理與 [該] 有效管理 [，承認原住民族與傳統領地（若適用）]，包括將氣候變遷考量與參與式風險評估納入物種與生態系保育，以及管理人類與野生動物衝突以促進共存，將其作為達成管理有效性之關鍵條件，包括保育共生地之範例與最佳實務；","html":"<p>保護區及保育共生地之規劃、治理與 [該] 有效管理 [，承認原住民族與傳統領地（若適用）]，包括將氣候變遷考量與參與式風險評估納入物種與生態系保育，以及管理人類與野生動物衝突以促進共存，將其作為達成管理有效性之關鍵條件，包括保育共生地之範例與最佳實務；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(viii)","html":"<p>(viii)</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"生態網絡、保育鑲嵌、具氣候資訊之空間規劃與廊道設計、不同尺度之生態連結性、跨境保育及其對和平之貢獻，以及復育，包括在城市與近郊背景下；","html":"<p>生態網絡、保育鑲嵌、具氣候資訊之空間規劃與廊道設計、不同尺度之生態連結性、跨境保育及其對和平之貢獻，以及復育，包括在城市與近郊背景下；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(ix)","html":"<p>(ix)</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"[保護區及保育共生地之監測與評估系統，承認原住民族與傳統領地（若適用）]，包括透過生物多樣性監測與相關新技術之使用、以社區為基礎之監測、強化國家生物多樣性資料庫等其他相關面向，且在可能情況下，遵循可發現、可存取、可互操作與可重複使用 (FAIR) 以及集體利益、控制權、責任與倫理 (CARE) 之原則 [, 並符合國家情況與立法]；","html":"<p>[保護區及保育共生地之監測與評估系統，承認原住民族與傳統領地（若適用）]，包括透過生物多樣性監測與相關新技術之使用、以社區為基礎之監測、強化國家生物多樣性資料庫等其他相關面向，且在可能情況下，遵循可發現、可存取、可互操作與可重複使用 (FAIR) 以及集體利益、控制權、責任與倫理 (CARE) 之原則 [, 並符合國家情況與立法]；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"(x)","html":"<p>(x)</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"與以下事項相關之永續金融方法、創新財務機制，包括來自公共與私人來源 [及環境與社會安全保障]：","html":"<p>與以下事項相關之永續金融方法、創新財務機制，包括來自公共與私人來源 [及環境與社會安全保障]：</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"---\n4 A/CONF.232/2023/4.","html":"<hr />\n<p>4 A/CONF.232/2023/4.</p>","en":[10,11]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p005.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"implementation of Target 3 of the Framework according to national priorities and in line with the implementation of their national biodiversity strategies and action plans, including direct and accessible financing approaches for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth;"},{"t":"(xi)       Good practices related to access to information, participation in decision-making, access to justice and the protection of environmental human rights defenders, consistent with Target 22 of the Framework;]"},{"t":"(d) To report on progress made in the implementation of the present decision to the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties."},{"t":"Annex"},{"t":"Update to the programme of work on [protected and conserved areas][protected areas and [areas with] other effective area-based conservation measures[, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]]"},{"t":"1.     The table below shows the mapping of the targets of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework5 against complementary activities that could support the implementation of the programme of work.6 It highlights areas of strong alignment, opportunities to strengthen existing provisions and gaps where further development is needed. It is based on the findings of a strategic review of the programme, related submissions and a peer review analysis. The activities are categorized as follows: (A) activities that have existing strong alignment with Target 3 of the Framework and its interlinkages with other targets; (B) activities that address targets that are partially covered by the programme of work and where implementation can be strengthened; and (C) activities for further developing areas that the programme of work does not cover or only covers in a limited manner and where additional guidance is needed. For Targets 9, 13, 16, 17 and 18, no specific actions [relevant to protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] are proposed."},{"t":"2.    The implementation of the updated programme of work should be conducted in line with section C of the Framework, [in particular by following a human rights-based approach,] and in accordance with national circumstances, legislation and priorities."},{"t":"I.     Complementary activities to strengthen the programme of work on [protected and conserved areas][protected areas and [areas with] other effective area-based conservation measures[, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]] and its alignment with the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework"},{"t":"Targets of the            Complementary activities                                                 Category\nKunming-Montreal\nGlobal Biodiversity\nFramework\nTarget 1                  1.     Integrate protected areas and other effective area-based          A","tb":1},{"t":"conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable, into broader landscape and seascape planning to improve, in accordance with national legislation, biodiversity outcomes, ecological representativeness and connectivity, through participatory and biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning"},{"t":"5 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"6 Decision VII/28, annex."},{"t":"5/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"(xi)\n根據國家優先事項，並與其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫的實施保持一致，實施綱要目標 3，包括為原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年提供直接且易於取得的財務方法；","html":"<p>(xi)<br />\n根據國家優先事項，並與其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫的實施保持一致，實施綱要目標 3，包括為原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年提供直接且易於取得的財務方法；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"與綱要目標 22 一致，關於資訊取得、參與決策、訴訟救濟以及保護環境人權捍衛者的良好實務；]","html":"<p>與綱要目標 22 一致，關於資訊取得、參與決策、訴訟救濟以及保護環境人權捍衛者的良好實務；]</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(d) 向科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構報告本決議實施進展，該會議應於第十八次締約方大會召開前舉行。","html":"<p>(d) 向科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構報告本決議實施進展，該會議應於第十八次締約方大會召開前舉行。</p>","en":[3,4]},{"md":"附件\n關於 [保護與保育區域][保護區與 [含有] 保育共生地[, 在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地]] 工作計畫之更新","html":"<p>附件<br />\n關於 [保護與保育區域][保護區與 [含有] 保育共生地[, 在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地]] 工作計畫之更新</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"1.\n下表顯示了昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要$^5$ 之目標與可支持工作計畫實施之補充活動之間的對應關係$^6$。此表強調了高度一致的領域、強化現有條款的機會，以及需要進一步開發的缺口。此表係基於對該工作計畫之策略性審查、相關提交文件及同儕審查分析之結果。活動分類如下：(A) 與綱要目標 3 及其與其他目標之相互關聯具有現有高度一致性的活動；(B) 針對工作計畫僅部分涵蓋且實施可望強化之目標的活動；以及 (C) 針對工作計畫未涵蓋或僅有限度涵蓋、且需要額外指引之領域進行進一步開發的活動。針對目標 9、13、16、17 及 18，未提出任何特定行動 [與保護區及保育共生地相關，且在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，]","html":"<p>1.<br />\n下表顯示了昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>5</sup> 之目標與可支持工作計畫實施之補充活動之間的對應關係<sup>6</sup>。此表強調了高度一致的領域、強化現有條款的機會，以及需要進一步開發的缺口。此表係基於對該工作計畫之策略性審查、相關提交文件及同儕審查分析之結果。活動分類如下：(A) 與綱要目標 3 及其與其他目標之相互關聯具有現有高度一致性的活動；(B) 針對工作計畫僅部分涵蓋且實施可望強化之目標的活動；以及 (C) 針對工作計畫未涵蓋或僅有限度涵蓋、且需要額外指引之領域進行進一步開發的活動。針對目標 9、13、16、17 及 18，未提出任何特定行動 [與保護區及保育共生地相關，且在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，]</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"2.\n更新後工作計畫的實施應與綱要 C 節保持一致，[特別是透過遵循以人權為基礎的方法，] 並符合國家情況、立法與優先事項。","html":"<p>2.<br />\n更新後工作計畫的實施應與綱要 C 節保持一致，[特別是透過遵循以人權為基礎的方法，] 並符合國家情況、立法與優先事項。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"I.\n強化關於 [保護與保育區域][保護區與 [含有] 保育共生地[, 在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地]] 之工作計畫及其與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要一致性之補充活動","html":"<p>I.<br />\n強化關於 [保護與保育區域][保護區與 [含有] 保育共生地[, 在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地]] 之工作計畫及其與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要一致性之補充活動</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"| 昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 目標 1 | 1. 透過參與式且具生物多樣性包容性的空間規劃，根據國家立法，將保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）整合至更廣泛的陸域與海域規劃中，以改善生物多樣性成果、生態代表性與連結性 | A |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">1. 透過參與式且具生物多樣性包容性的空間規劃，根據國家立法，將保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）整合至更廣泛的陸域與海域規劃中，以改善生物多樣性成果、生態代表性與連結性</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[9,10]},{"md":"---\n$^5$ 決議 15/4，附件。\n$^6$ 決議 VII/28，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>5</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n<sup>6</sup> 決議 VII/28，附件。</p>","en":[11,12,13]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c-v-4/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p006.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"Targets of the            Complementary activities                                                          Category","tb":1},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"processes, while recognizing and respecting the rights of indigenous peoples and local communities."},{"t":"[1 bis Identify and map, using best available science and, subject to free, prior and informed consent, as applicable, indigenous and local knowledge, ecological corridors, stepping-stones and other areas of particular importance for ecological connectivity, including for threatened and migratory species, and integrate this information into relevant national and subnational spatial planning policies, legislation, regulations and programmes, including for the designation and expansion of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable, paying particular attention to priority connectivity areas not yet integrated into such systems. 1.ter. Strengthen capacities on spatial tools and facilitate technical exchange on integrating ecological connectivity into terrestrial, aerial, freshwater, coastal and marine spatial planning processes.]"},{"t":"Target 2                  2.    Promote the restoration of degraded ecosystems [within                      B","tb":1},{"t":"protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], and beyond, including buffer zones, ecological corridors, soil biodiversity[, [including] fungal biodiversity,7] and inland water ecosystems, with a view to restoring ecological integrity and ecological connectivity across landscapes and seascapes, including through the development of criteria for identifying priority restoration areas and approaches for measuring restoration success, ensuring inclusive and gender-responsive implementation of the restoration efforts, as appropriate."},{"t":"[2.bis Scale up ecological connectivity measures within currently under-represented ecosystems, including marine and island ecosystems, rivers, wetlands, estuaries and coastal zones, and seek, as appropriate, to align terrestrial ecological corridors with riverine and inland water networks, in support of restoring ecological integrity and connectivity across landscapes and seascapes.]"},{"t":"Target 3                  3.    Incorporate the language, scope and timelines of Target 3 of the            A","tb":1},{"t":"Framework across implementation of the programme of work, updating relevant timelines and terminology, and ensuring coherence with related processes carried out under the Convention on Biological Diversity, including the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 2030.8"},{"t":"4.    Strengthen guidance related to improving monitoring, reporting and evaluation systems for terrestrial, inland waters, coastal and marine ecosystems to improve the assessment of biodiversity outcomes, including in relation to ecological representativeness, connectivity, integrity, conservation effectiveness, management effectiveness, governance quality, species population trends and through the use of appropriately indicators of the monitoring framework for the Kunming- Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,9 as well as disaggregated"},{"t":"7 As described in Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations and others, State of Knowledge of Soil Biodiversity:"},{"t":"Status, Challenges and Potentialities, Report 2020 (Rome, 2020)."},{"t":"8 Decision 16/4, annex."},{"t":"9 Decision 15/5, annex I, as updated in decision 16/31, and decision 17/-- on planning, monitoring, reporting and review."},{"t":"6/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"非正式文件（Non-paper）關於議程項目 17 (c) – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20\n昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標","html":"<p>非正式文件（Non-paper）關於議程項目 17 (c) – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20<br />\n昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"補充活動","html":"<p>補充活動</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"類別","html":"<p>類別</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"程序，同時承認並尊重原住民族與地方社區之權利。\n[1 bis 使用現有最佳科學，並在符合自由、事先及知情同意（視適用情況而定）的前提下，識別並繪製原住民與地方知識、生態廊道、踏腳石（stepping-stones）及其他對生態連結具有特別重要性之區域（包括針對受威脅物種與遷徙物種），並將此資訊整合至相關之國家與次國家級空間規劃政策、立法、法規與計畫中，包括用於指定與擴大保護區及保育共生地，並在適用情況下承認原住民與傳統領地，特別關注尚未整合至此類系統中之優先連結區域。\n1.ter. 強化空間工具之能力建構，並促進將生態連結整合至陸域、航空、淡水、沿岸及海洋空間規劃程序中之技術交流。]","html":"<p>程序，同時承認並尊重原住民族與地方社區之權利。<br />\n[1 bis 使用現有最佳科學，並在符合自由、事先及知情同意（視適用情況而定）的前提下，識別並繪製原住民與地方知識、生態廊道、踏腳石（stepping-stones）及其他對生態連結具有特別重要性之區域（包括針對受威脅物種與遷徙物種），並將此資訊整合至相關之國家與次國家級空間規劃政策、立法、法規與計畫中，包括用於指定與擴大保護區及保育共生地，並在適用情況下承認原住民與傳統領地，特別關注尚未整合至此類系統中之優先連結區域。<br />\n1.ter. 強化空間工具之能力建構，並促進將生態連結整合至陸域、航空、淡水、沿岸及海洋空間規劃程序中之技術交流。]</p>","en":[4,5,6]},{"md":"目標 2","html":"<p>目標 2</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"2.\n促進退化生態系之復育[在保護區及保育共生地內，並在適用情況下承認原住民與傳統領地]及除此之外之區域，包括緩衝區、生態廊道、土壤生物多樣性[[包括]真菌生物多樣性$^7$]及內陸水域生態系，旨在復育跨景觀與跨海域之生態完整性與生態連結，包括透過制定識別優先復育區域之標準以及衡量復育成功之方法，並在適當情況下，確保復育工作之執行具備包容性與性別回應性。\n[2.bis 在目前代表性不足之生態系中擴大生態連結措施，包括海洋與島嶼生態系、河流、濕地、河口及沿岸地帶，並在適當情況下，尋求使陸域生態廊道與河川及內陸水域網絡一致，以支持復育跨景觀與跨海域之生態完整性與連結性。]","html":"<p>2.<br />\n促進退化生態系之復育[在保護區及保育共生地內，並在適用情況下承認原住民與傳統領地]及除此之外之區域，包括緩衝區、生態廊道、土壤生物多樣性[[包括]真菌生物多樣性<sup>7</sup>]及內陸水域生態系，旨在復育跨景觀與跨海域之生態完整性與生態連結，包括透過制定識別優先復育區域之標準以及衡量復育成功之方法，並在適當情況下，確保復育工作之執行具備包容性與性別回應性。<br />\n[2.bis 在目前代表性不足之生態系中擴大生態連結措施，包括海洋與島嶼生態系、河流、濕地、河口及沿岸地帶，並在適當情況下，尋求使陸域生態廊道與河川及內陸水域網絡一致，以支持復育跨景觀與跨海域之生態完整性與連結性。]</p>","en":[8,9]},{"md":"B","html":"<p>B</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"目標 3","html":"<p>目標 3</p>","pre":"跨海域之生態完整性與連結性。]\n\nB\n\n","en":[10]},{"md":"3.\n在工作計畫之執行過程中，納入綱要目標 3 之用語、範圍與時程，更新相關時程與術語，並確保與《生物多樣性公約》下進行之相關程序保持一致，包括關於第 8(j) 條及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關規定之工作計畫至 2030 年$^8$。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n在工作計畫之執行過程中，納入綱要目標 3 之用語、範圍與時程，更新相關時程與術語，並確保與《生物多樣性公約》下進行之相關程序保持一致，包括關於第 8(j) 條及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關規定之工作計畫至 2030 年<sup>8</sup>。</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"4.\n強化與改善陸域、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系監測、報告與評估系統相關之指引，以改善生物多樣性成果之評估，包括關於生態代表性、連結性、完整性、保育成效、管理成效、治理品質、物種族群趨勢之評估，並透過使用昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構之適當指標$^9$，以及透過分項資料……","html":"<p>4.<br />\n強化與改善陸域、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系監測、報告與評估系統相關之指引，以改善生物多樣性成果之評估，包括關於生態代表性、連結性、完整性、保育成效、管理成效、治理品質、物種族群趨勢之評估，並透過使用昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構之適當指標<sup>9</sup>，以及透過分項資料……</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"---\n$^7$ 如聯合國糧食及農業組織（FAO）及其他機構所載，《土壤生物多樣性現況：地位、挑戰與潛力，2020 年報告》（羅馬，2020）。\n$^8$ 決議 16/4，附件。\n$^9$ 決議 15/5，附件 I，經決議 16/31 更新，以及關於規劃、監測、報告與審查之決議 17/--。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>7</sup> 如聯合國糧食及農業組織（FAO）及其他機構所載，《土壤生物多樣性現況：地位、挑戰與潛力，2020 年報告》（羅馬，2020）。<br />\n<sup>8</sup> 決議 16/4，附件。<br />\n<sup>9</sup> 決議 15/5，附件 I，經決議 16/31 更新，以及關於規劃、監測、報告與審查之決議 17/--。</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c-v-4/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p007.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"Targets of the            Complementary activities                                                             Category","tb":1},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"indicators, including, as appropriate, by ecosystem type and level of protection."},{"t":"5.     Enhance guidance related to the recognition, respect, promotion and protection of indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable, in the context of Target 3 of the Framework, in a manner consistent with the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities. This encompasses differentiated approaches to ensure comprehensive protection, including for indigenous peoples in voluntary isolation and initial contact, in line with the principles of no contact, intangibility and precaution, in accordance with national circumstances."},{"t":"6.     Increase the uptake of practical frameworks, guidance, emerging innovative tools, case studies and national experiences, lessons learned and different approaches to support the implementation of Target 3 of the Framework, including the definition and prioritization of areas of particular importance for biodiversity, ecological networks, corridor design for climate adaptation, large‑scale ecological connectivity, including ecological processes below ground, other effective area-based conservation measures and transboundary conservation."},{"t":"7.     Strengthen the operationalization of equitable and effective governance in planning and management [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] [and a human rights-based approach] consistent with section C of the Framework, including by, as appropriate, shifting from beneficiary‑based approaches to recognizing, respecting, promoting and protecting the rights and contributions of indigenous peoples and local communities; promoting standards and good practices for participation, shared governance and co‑management arrangements; ensuring culturally appropriate access to information; respecting and strengthening, where applicable, the implementation of free, prior and informed consent,10 consistent with national circumstances and legislation and relevant international instruments."},{"t":"8.     Strengthen inclusive monitoring, reporting and evaluation systems [for protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including by identifying available tools, and facilitate the use of relevant new technologies to better assess ecological representativeness, integrity and connectivity, biodiversity outcomes, management effectiveness, governance quality, species population trends, relevant indicators of the monitoring framework, as well as relevant disaggregated indicators."},{"t":"9.     Promote the use of relevant and new approaches for ecological integrity and connectivity in the planning and management [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including through the development of ecological networks, ecological corridors, stepping stones and transboundary connectivity initiatives"},{"t":"10 “Free, prior and informed consent” refers to the tripartite terminology of “prior and informed consent”, “free, prior and"},{"t":"informed consent” and “approval and involvement”."},{"t":"7/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"**昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標**","html":"<p><strong>昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標</strong></p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**補充活動**","html":"<p><strong>補充活動</strong></p>","en":[5]},{"md":"| 類別 | 指標，包括視情況按生態系類型與保護等級分類。 |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| | 5. 在綱要目標 3 的脈絡下，強化與承認、尊重、促進及保護原住民族與傳統領地相關之指引（如適用），其方式應與關於第 8(j) 條之工作計畫，以及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關之規定保持一致。這包括採取差異化方法以確保全面性的保護，包括針對處於自願隔離與初步接觸狀態的原住民族，並應符合不接觸、不可侵犯及預防原則，並根據國家情況辦理。 |\n| | 6. 增加實務框架、指引、新興創新工具、個案研究、國家經驗、經驗教訓及不同方法的運用，以支持綱要目標 3 的實施，包括對生物多樣性特別重要區域的定義與優先排序、生態網絡、氣候適應之廊道設計、大規模生態連結性（包括地下生態過程）、保育共生地以及跨境保育。 |\n| | 7. 強化在規劃與管理 [保護區及保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地，] [以及採取以人權為基礎之方法] 中，落實公平且有效的治理，且應與綱要 C 節保持一致，包括視情況從以受益者為基礎的方法，轉向承認、尊重、促進及保護原住民族與地方社區之權利與貢獻；促進參與、共同治理與共同管理安排之標準與良好實務；確保文化適切之資訊取得；在符合國家情況、立法及相關國際文書之情況下，尊重並強化（如適用）自由、事先及知情同意之實施。¹⁰ |\n| | 8. 強化具包容性的監測、報告與評估系統 [針對保護區及保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過識別可用工具，並促進相關新技術之使用，以更佳地評估生態代表性、完整性與連結性、生物多樣性成果、管理成效、治理品質、物種族群趨勢、監測架構之相關指標，以及相關的分層指標。 |\n| | 9. 在規劃與管理 [保護區及保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地] 的過程中，促進用於生態完整性與連結性的相關及新方法，包括透過開發生態網絡、生態廊道、踏腳石（stepping stones）及跨境連結性倡議。 |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指標，包括視情況按生態系類型與保護等級分類。</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">5. 在綱要目標 3 的脈絡下，強化與承認、尊重、促進及保護原住民族與傳統領地相關之指引（如適用），其方式應與關於第 8(j) 條之工作計畫，以及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關之規定保持一致。這包括採取差異化方法以確保全面性的保護，包括針對處於自願隔離與初步接觸狀態的原住民族，並應符合不接觸、不可侵犯及預防原則，並根據國家情況辦理。</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">6. 增加實務框架、指引、新興創新工具、個案研究、國家經驗、經驗教訓及不同方法的運用，以支持綱要目標 3 的實施，包括對生物多樣性特別重要區域的定義與優先排序、生態網絡、氣候適應之廊道設計、大規模生態連結性（包括地下生態過程）、保育共生地以及跨境保育。</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">7. 強化在規劃與管理 [保護區及保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地，] [以及採取以人權為基礎之方法] 中，落實公平且有效的治理，且應與綱要 C 節保持一致，包括視情況從以受益者為基礎的方法，轉向承認、尊重、促進及保護原住民族與地方社區之權利與貢獻；促進參與、共同治理與共同管理安排之標準與良好實務；確保文化適切之資訊取得；在符合國家情況、立法及相關國際文書之情況下，尊重並強化（如適用）自由、事先及知情同意之實施。¹⁰</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">8. 強化具包容性的監測、報告與評估系統 [針對保護區及保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過識別可用工具，並促進相關新技術之使用，以更佳地評估生態代表性、完整性與連結性、生物多樣性成果、管理成效、治理品質、物種族群趨勢、監測架構之相關指標，以及相關的分層指標。</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">9. 在規劃與管理 [保護區及保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地] 的過程中，促進用於生態完整性與連結性的相關及新方法，包括透過開發生態網絡、生態廊道、踏腳石（stepping stones）及跨境連結性倡議。</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"¹⁰「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。","html":"<p>¹⁰「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。</p>","en":[11,12,13]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c-v-4/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p008.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"Targets of the         Complementary activities                                                   Category","tb":1},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"and corridor design for climate adaptation across wider landscapes and seascapes."},{"t":"10. Strengthen the integration of climate change considerations into the planning and management of [protected and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including ecological corridors. [10 bis. Draft, adopt or strengthen, in accordance with national legislation, measures that recognize ecological networks, corridors, stepping-stones and other areas of particular importance for connectivity, and support their management in ways that allow for the movement of species and the flow of ecological processes across and beyond [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable."},{"t":"[10 bis Alt. [Consider the][Adopt and] strengthening in accordance [with national circumstances] and legislation measures that recognize ecological networks, corridors, stepping stones and other areas [as] of particular importance for connectivity and support their management in ways that allow for the movement of species and the flow of ecological processes across [and beyond] [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]]] 10.ter Co-develop, as appropriate, with financial institutions, the private sector and relevant partners, financing approaches, incentives and risk assessments that take into account ecological connectivity, in order to mobilize resources for the maintenance, enhancement and restoration of ecological connectivity across [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable] and their surrounding landscapes and seascapes."},{"t":"10.quart Map existing long-distance trails with ecological connectivity roles, generate research and develop guidelines for implementation of long-distance trails as conservation tools, engage with long distance trail managers and provide capacity building strategies on connectivity, associated with long distance trails for their managers. 10 quinquies. Strengthen capacity-building, technical and scientific cooperation, and knowledge exchange on planning, management and financing related to ecological connectivity, inclusive and equitable governance models for ecological networks and corridors, including at landscape- and seascape-scales and with attention to the rights of indigenous peoples and local communities, and for the integration of ecological connectivity into national biodiversity strategies and action plans (NBSAPs), sectoral policies and implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework. 10 sexties. Integrate social, cultural, recreational, and economic considerations into ecological connectivity measures and, where appropriate and feasible, address their positive and negative impacts promoting collaborative landscape- and seascape-scale governance mechanisms linking protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable with surrounding uses.]"},{"t":"8/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"**昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標**","html":"<p><strong>昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標</strong></p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**跨越更廣泛之陸域與海域景觀以進行氣候適應的補充活動與廊道設計**","html":"<p><strong>跨越更廣泛之陸域與海域景觀以進行氣候適應的補充活動與廊道設計</strong></p>","en":[6]},{"md":"10. 強化將氣候變遷考量納入 [保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）] 之規劃與管理，包括生態廊道。","html":"<p>10. 強化將氣候變遷考量納入 [保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）] 之規劃與管理，包括生態廊道。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"[10 bis. 根據國家立法，起草、採納或強化旨在承認生態網絡、廊道、踏腳石及其他對連通性具有特殊重要性之區域的措施，並支持其管理方式，以允許物種移動及生態過程在 [保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）] 之內及之外進行流動。","html":"<p>[10 bis. 根據國家立法，起草、採納或強化旨在承認生態網絡、廊道、踏腳石及其他對連通性具有特殊重要性之區域的措施，並支持其管理方式，以允許物種移動及生態過程在 [保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）] 之內及之外進行流動。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"[10 bis 替代方案：[考慮][採納與] 根據 [依據國家情況] 及立法，強化旨在承認生態網絡、廊道、踏腳石及其他 [作為] 對連通性具有特殊重要性之區域的措施，並支持其管理方式，以允許物種移動及生態過程在 [保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）] 之內 [及之外] 進行流動]","html":"<p>[10 bis 替代方案：[考慮][採納與] 根據 [依據國家情況] 及立法，強化旨在承認生態網絡、廊道、踏腳石及其他 [作為] 對連通性具有特殊重要性之區域的措施，並支持其管理方式，以允許物種移動及生態過程在 [保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）] 之內 [及之外] 進行流動]</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"10.ter 視適當情況，與金融機構、私營部門及相關夥伴共同開發考量生態連通性的融資方法、激勵措施與風險評估，以動員資源用於維護、增強及復育 [保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）] 及其周邊陸域與海域景觀之生態連通性。","html":"<p>10.ter 視適當情況，與金融機構、私營部門及相關夥伴共同開發考量生態連通性的融資方法、激勵措施與風險評估，以動員資源用於維護、增強及復育 [保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）] 及其周邊陸域與海域景觀之生態連通性。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"10.quart 繪製具有生態連通性功能之現有長距離步道地圖，進行研究並制定將長距離步道作為保育工具之實施指南，與長距離步道管理者進行交流，並為其管理者提供與長距離步道相關之連通性能力建構策略。","html":"<p>10.quart 繪製具有生態連通性功能之現有長距離步道地圖，進行研究並制定將長距離步道作為保育工具之實施指南，與長距離步道管理者進行交流，並為其管理者提供與長距離步道相關之連通性能力建構策略。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"10 quinquies. 強化關於生態連通性規劃、管理與融資、生態網絡與廊道之包容且公平之治理模式（包括在陸域與海域景觀尺度上，並關注原住民族與地方社區之權利），以及將生態連通性納入國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫 (NBSAPs)、部門政策及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》實施之技術與科學合作及知識交流、能力建構。","html":"<p>10 quinquies. 強化關於生態連通性規劃、管理與融資、生態網絡與廊道之包容且公平之治理模式（包括在陸域與海域景觀尺度上，並關注原住民族與地方社區之權利），以及將生態連通性納入國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫 (NBSAPs)、部門政策及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》實施之技術與科學合作及知識交流、能力建構。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"10 sexties. 將社會、文化、休閒與經濟考量納入生態連通性措施中，並在適當且可行之情況下，處理其正面與負面影響，以促進連結保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）與周邊利用之協作式陸域與海域景觀尺度治理機制]。","html":"<p>10 sexties. 將社會、文化、休閒與經濟考量納入生態連通性措施中，並在適當且可行之情況下，處理其正面與負面影響，以促進連結保護區與保育共生地（在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地）與周邊利用之協作式陸域與海域景觀尺度治理機制]。</p>","en":[8]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c-v-4/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p009.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"Targets of the           Complementary activities                                                       Category\nKunming-Montreal\nGlobal Biodiversity\nFramework\nTarget 4                 11. Strengthen capacities for planning and management through                  B","tb":1},{"t":"participatory risk assessment, rapid response mechanisms, where possible, and inclusive community engagements and the integration of traditional knowledge in addressing human-wildlife conflict and promoting coexistence[ in protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]."},{"t":"12. Integrate effective management of human-wildlife interactions, including human-wildlife conflict risk assessment, in order to minimize conflict to promote coexistence [in the context of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]. [12 bis Strengthen the development and implementation of national and, where appropriate, site-specific species action or recovery plans for threatened species, including provisions for population monitoring, threat abatement, habitat management, and the maintenance and restoration of ecological connectivity, including through ecological corridors, within and beyond protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable, in accordance with national legislation, priorities and available resources.]"},{"t":"Target 5                 13. Address and manage the use of wild species [within protected               B\n                         areas and other effective area-based conservation measures,\n                         recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,]\n                         where such use is allowed, in a manner that mitigates risks to native\n                         biodiversity and human health, consistent with site‑specific\n                         conservation objectives and zoning, while preventing overexploitation\n                         and ensuring sustainable, legal and safe use at all stages, including\n                         through participatory biodiversity monitoring and the application of\n                         One Health risk assessment frameworks, as appropriate, and respecting\n                         and protecting the customary sustainable use practices of indigenous\n                         peoples and local communities.\nTarget 6                 14. Strengthen the prediction, prevention, early detection, control or         B\n                         eradication of and the rapid response to invasive alien species [in\n                         protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures,\n                         recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable],\n                         including through community-based monitoring, surveillance systems,\n                         and biosecurity and trade-related measures.11\n                         15. Strengthen guidelines, where applicable, for the development and\n                         implementation of national and regional plans for the management of\n                         invasive alien species and pathways of introduction into protected\n                         areas.\nTarget 7                 16. Address pollution pressures from all sources [affecting] protected         B\n                         areas and other effective area-based conservation measures,\n                         recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,\n                         cumulative impacts and land-sea interactions.\nTarget 8                 17. Strengthen the integration of climate change considerations into           C","tb":1},{"t":"the planning and management of [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures recognizing indigenous and"},{"t":"11 Any international measures should be implemented in compliance with the Agreement on the Application of Sanitary and"},{"t":"Phytosanitary Measures of the World Trade Organization and with the International Plant Protection Convention."},{"t":"9/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"**昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標**","html":"<p><strong>昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標</strong></p>","en":[0]},{"md":"| 目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **目標 4** | 11. 透過參與式風險評估、在可能的情況下建立快速反應機制、包容性的社區參與，以及在處理人類與野生動物衝突與促進共存時整合傳統知識，來強化規劃與管理之能力 [在保護區與保育共生地中，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]。<br><br>12. 整合人類與野生動物互動之有效管理，包括人類與野生動物衝突風險評估，以將衝突降至最低並促進共存 [在保護區與保育共生地的脈絡下，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]。<br><br>[12 bis 強化針對受威脅物種之國家級及（在適當情況下）特定場域物種行動或復育計畫的制定與執行，包括針對族群監測、威脅減緩、棲地管理，以及透過保護區與保育共生地內外的生態廊道來維持與復育生態連結之規定，在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地，並符合國家立法、優先事項及可用資源。] | B |\n| **目標 5** | 13. 在允許該種利用的情況下，處理並管理野生物種之利用 [在保護區與保育共生地內，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地，] 以降低對原生生物多樣性與人類健康之風險，並與特定場域之保育目標及分區規劃保持一致，同時防止過度開發，並確保在所有階段皆為永續、合法且安全之利用，包括透過參與式生物多樣性監測以及適當應用健康一體風險評估架構，並尊重且保護原住民族與地方社區之慣習性永續利用實務。 | B |\n| **目標 6** | 14. 強化對外來入侵種之預測、預防、早期偵測、控制或根除，以及快速反應 [在保護區與保育共生地中，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過以社區為基礎的監測、監控系統，以及生物安全與貿易相關措施。¹¹<br><br>15. 在適用情況下，強化針對管理外來入侵種及其進入保護區之路徑的國家與區域計畫之制定與執行指南。 | B |\n| **目標 7** | 16. 處理來自所有來源對 [影響] 保護區與保育共生地之污染壓力（在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地）、累積影響及陸海互動。 | B |\n| **目標 8** | 17. 強化將氣候變遷考量納入 [保護區與保育共生地之規劃與管理中，並在承認原住民族與... | C |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">11. 透過參與式風險評估、在可能的情況下建立快速反應機制、包容性的社區參與，以及在處理人類與野生動物衝突與促進共存時整合傳統知識，來強化規劃與管理之能力 [在保護區與保育共生地中，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]。<br><br>12. 整合人類與野生動物互動之有效管理，包括人類與野生動物衝突風險評估，以將衝突降至最低並促進共存 [在保護區與保育共生地的脈絡下，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]。<br><br>[12 bis 強化針對受威脅物種之國家級及（在適當情況下）特定場域物種行動或復育計畫的制定與執行，包括針對族群監測、威脅減緩、棲地管理，以及透過保護區與保育共生地內外的生態廊道來維持與復育生態連結之規定，在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地，並符合國家立法、優先事項及可用資源。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 5</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">13. 在允許該種利用的情況下，處理並管理野生物種之利用 [在保護區與保育共生地內，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地，] 以降低對原生生物多樣性與人類健康之風險，並與特定場域之保育目標及分區規劃保持一致，同時防止過度開發，並確保在所有階段皆為永續、合法且安全之利用，包括透過參與式生物多樣性監測以及適當應用健康一體風險評估架構，並尊重且保護原住民族與地方社區之慣習性永續利用實務。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 6</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">14. 強化對外來入侵種之預測、預防、早期偵測、控制或根除，以及快速反應 [在保護區與保育共生地中，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過以社區為基礎的監測、監控系統，以及生物安全與貿易相關措施。¹¹<br><br>15. 在適用情況下，強化針對管理外來入侵種及其進入保護區之路徑的國家與區域計畫之制定與執行指南。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 7</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">16. 處理來自所有來源對 [影響] 保護區與保育共生地之污染壓力（在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地）、累積影響及陸海互動。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 8</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">17. 強化將氣候變遷考量納入 [保護區與保育共生地之規劃與管理中，並在承認原住民族與...</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">C</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"¹¹ 任何國際措施之實施，均應符合世界貿易組織《衛生與植物衛生措施協議》及《國際植物保護公約》。","html":"<p>¹¹ 任何國際措施之實施，均應符合世界貿易組織《衛生與植物衛生措施協議》及《國際植物保護公約》。</p>","en":[6,7,8]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c-v-4/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p010.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"Targets of the         Complementary activities                                                      Category","tb":1},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"traditional territories, where applicable], including ecological corridors, by scaling up related response measures that promote resilience in order to minimize the negative impacts of climate change, while ensuring ecological integrity."},{"t":"18. Promote system design for climate adaptation and resilience that anticipates future range shifts, including by identifying additional climate refugia, connectivity corridors, soil biodiversity, [including but not limited to fungal biodiversity,] and areas of future biodiversity importance."},{"t":"Target 9               [19. No specific actions identified.]                                         [n/a]\nTarget 10              20. Strengthen guidance on how the sustainable management of                  C\n                       productive landscapes and biodiversity-friendly practices can support\n                       ecological connectivity, ecosystem functions and resilience across\n                       landscapes and seascapes and biodiversity improvements for protected\n                       areas and other effective area-based conservation measures,\n                       recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable and\n                       how these areas can contribute towards and in line with Target 3 of the\n                       Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework\nTarget 11              21. Highlight the role of [protected areas and other effective area-          B\n                       based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional\n                       territories, where applicable,] in restoring, maintaining and enhancing\n                       nature’s contributions to people, including ecosystem functions and\n                       services, as well as strengthen capacities to measure and value those\n                       functions and services.\nTarget 12              22. Integrate [protected areas and other effective area-based                 C","tb":1},{"t":"conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] into urban and peri-urban planning, including through green and blue infrastructure, to enhance ecological connectivity, restoration, the conservation of native species and climate change adaptation, and to support physical and mental health and well-being, and equitable access to nature especially for the most vulnerable."},{"t":"[22. bis Support the integration of ecological networks, corridors and stepping-stones into urban and peri-urban spatial planning, including through green and blue infrastructure and buffer zones linking [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable] to surrounding landscapes and seascapes, in order to maintain ecological processes while enhancing equitable access to nature.]"},{"t":"Target 13              [23. No specific actions identified.]                                         [n/a]\nTarget 14              24. Integrate [protected areas and other effective area-based                 B\n                       conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional\n                       territories, where applicable,] into cross‑sectoral policies, legislation,\n                       planning and development processes, where relevant for their planning\n                       and effective management.\nTarget 15              25. Support and promote the implementation of legal, administrative           B","tb":1},{"t":"or policy measures that encourage and enable businesses and financial institutions to assess, disclose and progressively reduce biodiversity‑related risks, dependencies and impacts [on protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,]"},{"t":"10/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"**昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標**","html":"<p><strong>昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標</strong></p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**補充活動**","html":"<p><strong>補充活動</strong></p>","en":[5]},{"md":"| 目標 | 類別 | 活動內容 |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| **目標 9** | [n/a] | 傳統領地（如適用）]，包括生態廊道，透過擴大相關應對措施，以促進韌性，從而將氣候變遷的負面影響降至最低，同時確保生態完整性。 |\n| | | 18. 促進氣候調適與韌性的系統設計，以預測未來的分布範圍偏移，包括透過識別額外的氣候避難所、連通廊道、土壤生物多樣性、[包括但不限於真菌生物多樣性，] 以及未來具生物多樣性重要性的區域。<br>[19. 未識別出特定行動。] |\n| **目標 10** | C | 20. 加強關於如何透過生產性景觀的永續管理與生物多樣性友善做法，來支持跨陸域與海域的生態連通性、生態系功能與韌性，以及改善保護區與保育共生地之生物多樣性，並承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用），以及這些區域如何能與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 3 一致並對其做出貢獻，強化相關指引。 |\n| **目標 11** | B | 21. 強調[保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用），]在復育、維護與增強自然對人類的貢獻（包括生態系功能與服務）方面之角色，並強化衡量與評估該等功能與服務之能力。 |\n| **目標 12** | C | 22. 將[保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用），]整合至城市與近郊規劃中，包括透過綠色與藍色基礎設施，以增強生態連通性、復育、原生種保育與氣候變遷調適，並支持生理與心理健康與福祉，以及自然之公平取得，特別是針對最脆弱族群。<br>[22. bis 支持將生態網絡、廊道與踏腳石整合至城市與近郊空間規劃中，包括透過綠色與藍性基礎設施及緩衝區，將[保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用）]與周邊陸域及海域相連結，以在增強自然之公平取得之同時，維持生態過程。] |\n| **目標 13** | [n/a] | [23. 未識別出特定行動。] |\n| **目標 14** | B | 24. 將[保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用），]整合至跨部門政策、立法、規劃與發展程序中，只要其規劃與有效管理有所涉及。 |\n| **目標 15** | B | 25. 支持並促進法律、行政或政策措施之實施，以鼓勵並使企業與金融機構能夠評估、揭露並逐步減少與生物多樣性相關之風險、依賴性與影響[對於保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用）]。 |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">類別</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">活動內容</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 9</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">[n/a]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">傳統領地（如適用）]，包括生態廊道，透過擴大相關應對措施，以促進韌性，從而將氣候變遷的負面影響降至最低，同時確保生態完整性。</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">18. 促進氣候調適與韌性的系統設計，以預測未來的分布範圍偏移，包括透過識別額外的氣候避難所、連通廊道、土壤生物多樣性、[包括但不限於真菌生物多樣性，] 以及未來具生物多樣性重要性的區域。<br>[19. 未識別出特定行動。]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 10</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">C</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">20. 加強關於如何透過生產性景觀的永續管理與生物多樣性友善做法，來支持跨陸域與海域的生態連通性、生態系功能與韌性，以及改善保護區與保育共生地之生物多樣性，並承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用），以及這些區域如何能與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 3 一致並對其做出貢獻，強化相關指引。</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 11</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">B</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">21. 強調[保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用），]在復育、維護與增強自然對人類的貢獻（包括生態系功能與服務）方面之角色，並強化衡量與評估該等功能與服務之能力。</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 12</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">C</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">22. 將[保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用），]整合至城市與近郊規劃中，包括透過綠色與藍色基礎設施，以增強生態連通性、復育、原生種保育與氣候變遷調適，並支持生理與心理健康與福祉，以及自然之公平取得，特別是針對最脆弱族群。<br>[22. bis 支持將生態網絡、廊道與踏腳石整合至城市與近郊空間規劃中，包括透過綠色與藍性基礎設施及緩衝區，將[保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用）]與周邊陸域及海域相連結，以在增強自然之公平取得之同時，維持生態過程。]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 13</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">[n/a]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[23. 未識別出特定行動。]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 14</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">B</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">24. 將[保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用），]整合至跨部門政策、立法、規劃與發展程序中，只要其規劃與有效管理有所涉及。</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 15</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">B</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">25. 支持並促進法律、行政或政策措施之實施，以鼓勵並使企業與金融機構能夠評估、揭露並逐步減少與生物多樣性相關之風險、依賴性與影響[對於保護區與保育共生地，承認原住民族與傳統領地（如適用）]。</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c-v-4/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p011.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"Targets of the        Complementary activities                                                    Category\nKunming-Montreal\nGlobal Biodiversity\nFramework\n                      including across their operations, supply and value chains and\n                      portfolios, in order to promote sustainable value chains and reduce\n                      risks to biodiversity.\n                      26. Facilitate clearer direction on engaging financial actors and the\n                      private sector [in support of protected areas and other effective area-\n                      based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional\n                      territories, where applicable,] on a voluntary basis to develop the field\n                      of conservation, protection and restoration as a key economic area.\nTarget 16             27. Promote synergies between the policies and actions taken to             [n/a]\n                      protect and conserve biodiversity, and policies and actions in order to\n                      implement Target 16, including through coherent policy frameworks,\n                      education, access to reliable information and sector specific\n                      approaches, such as sustainable tourism management, contributing to\n                      the reduction of waste generation.\nTarget 17             [28. No specific actions identified.]                                       [n/a]\nTarget 18             [29. No specific actions identified.]                                       [n/a]\nTarget 19             30. Promote the identification of timely, predictable and accessible        A","tb":1},{"t":"financial resources from all sources, including domestic, international, public and private resources, for the effective implementation and long-term financial sustainability and institutional resilience [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] in accordance with Article 20 of the Convention and Target 19 of the Framework, and innovative mechanisms, such as public-private partnerships, especially to support developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States among them, consistent with national priorities and with environmental and social safeguards."},{"t":"31. Promote [direct and] accessible financing for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, where applicable under Target 3 of the Framework, in accordance with national circumstances."},{"t":"Target 20             32. Strengthen capacity-building and development, technical and             A\n                      scientific cooperation and technology transfer, on mutually agreed\n                      terms, for establishing and managing [protected areas and other\n                      effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous\n                      and traditional territories, where applicable], including with respect to\n                      new technologies and institutional support for the conservation\n                      workforce, such as rangers and other relevant personnel.\nTarget 21             33. Strengthen the application of advances in biodiversity                  B","tb":1},{"t":"monitoring, data management and knowledge‑sharing through targeted capacity‑building and development on comprehensive biodiversity monitoring and the use of innovative technologies, including digital technologies, remote sensing and national biodiversity databases, to improve monitoring, evaluation, reporting and decision‑making including regarding the implementation of Target 3 and relating to [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] including through nationally appropriate approaches and indicators, while strengthening capacities and infrastructure for managing and integrating biodiversity data."},{"t":"11/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"**昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標**","html":"<p><strong>昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標</strong></p>","en":[0]},{"md":"| 目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| | 包括在其營運、供應鏈、價值鏈及投資組合中，以促進永續價值鏈並降低對生物多樣性的風險。 | |\n| | 26. 促進更明確的方向，以自願方式吸引金融參與者及私營部門參與 [以支持保護區及保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，] 以將保育、保護與復育領域發展為關鍵經濟領域。 | |\n| **目標 16** | 27. 促進保護與保育生物多樣性所採取的政策與行動，以及為了執行目標 16 所採取的政策與行動之間的綜效，包括透過一致的政策框架、教育、取得可靠資訊以及特定產業的方法（例如永續旅遊管理），以促進廢棄物減量。 | [n/a] |\n| **目標 17** | [28. 未確定具體行動。] | [n/a] |\n| **目標 18** | [29. 未確定具體行動。] | [n/a] |\n| **目標 19** | 30. 促進從所有來源（包括國內、國際、公共及私人資源）識別及時、可預測且可取得之財務資源，以確保根據《公約》第 20 條及《綱要》目標 19，實現 [保護區及保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，] 的有效執行、長期財務永續性與制度韌性，並利用創新機制（例如公私夥伴關係），特別是為了支持開發中國家締約方，尤其是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，且須符合國家優先事項及環境與社會安全保障。 | |\n| | 31. 促進 [直接且] 可取得的資金，用於《綱要》目標 3 下在適用情況下針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，並符合國家情況。 | A |\n| **目標 20** | 32. 在共同商定的條件下，加強能力建構與發展、技術與科學合作以及技術轉移，以建立及管理 [保護區及保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括針對新技術以及為保育人力（如巡守員及其他相關人員）提供制度支持。 | A |\n| **目標 21** | 33. 透過針對全面性生物多樣性監測及創新技術使用（包括數位技術、遙測及國家生物多樣性資料庫）的定向能力建構與發展，加強生物多樣性監測、資料管理與知識共享之應用，以改善監測、評估、報告與決策（包括關於目標 3 之執行，以及涉及 [保護區及保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，] 之事項），並透過國家適當的方法與指標，同時加強管理與整合生物多樣性資料之能力與基礎設施。 | B |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">包括在其營運、供應鏈、價值鏈及投資組合中，以促進永續價值鏈並降低對生物多樣性的風險。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">26. 促進更明確的方向，以自願方式吸引金融參與者及私營部門參與 [以支持保護區及保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，] 以將保育、保護與復育領域發展為關鍵經濟領域。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 16</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">27. 促進保護與保育生物多樣性所採取的政策與行動，以及為了執行目標 16 所採取的政策與行動之間的綜效，包括透過一致的政策框架、教育、取得可靠資訊以及特定產業的方法（例如永續旅遊管理），以促進廢棄物減量。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[n/a]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 17</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[28. 未確定具體行動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[n/a]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 18</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[29. 未確定具體行動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[n/a]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 19</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">30. 促進從所有來源（包括國內、國際、公共及私人資源）識別及時、可預測且可取得之財務資源，以確保根據《公約》第 20 條及《綱要》目標 19，實現 [保護區及保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，] 的有效執行、長期財務永續性與制度韌性，並利用創新機制（例如公私夥伴關係），特別是為了支持開發中國家締約方，尤其是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，且須符合國家優先事項及環境與社會安全保障。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">31. 促進 [直接且] 可取得的資金，用於《綱要》目標 3 下在適用情況下針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，並符合國家情況。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 20</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">32. 在共同商定的條件下，加強能力建構與發展、技術與科學合作以及技術轉移，以建立及管理 [保護區及保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括針對新技術以及為保育人力（如巡守員及其他相關人員）提供制度支持。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 21</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">33. 透過針對全面性生物多樣性監測及創新技術使用（包括數位技術、遙測及國家生物多樣性資料庫）的定向能力建構與發展，加強生物多樣性監測、資料管理與知識共享之應用，以改善監測、評估、報告與決策（包括關於目標 3 之執行，以及涉及 [保護區及保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，] 之事項），並透過國家適當的方法與指標，同時加強管理與整合生物多樣性資料之能力與基礎設施。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c-v-4/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p012.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"Targets of the            Complementary activities                                                             Category\nKunming-Montreal\nGlobal Biodiversity\nFramework\nTarget 22                 34. Strengthen access to information and the full, equitable,                        B","tb":1},{"t":"inclusive, effective and gender-responsive representation and participation of indigenous peoples and local communities in decision-making related to protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable."},{"t":"35. [Ensure][Promote where possible] access to justice by indigenous peoples and local communities, women, children, youth and persons with disabilities, [ and promote the establishment of effective and accessible grievance mechanisms,] in accordance with national legislation and other relevant international agreements, to address issues related to the establishment, management and governance of [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]."},{"t":"36. [Ensure][Promote where possible] the full protection of environmental human rights defenders engaged in activities related to [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], [and in accordance with national legislation, and relevant international instruments and obligations]"},{"t":"Target 23                 37. Promote gender equality and integrate a gender-responsive                        A","tb":1},{"t":"approach, including the use of [disaggregated data by sex] and other relevant disaggregated indicators, in accordance with national legislation, across the programme of work [taking gender-based violence into due consideration]."},{"t":"[II. Programme element 5: ecological connectivity"},{"t":"Objective"},{"t":"3.     To maintain, enhance and restore structural and functional ecological connectivity across terrestrial, inland water, coastal and marine ecosystems, including by integrating ecologically representative and well-connected systems [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] into wider landscapes and seascapes."},{"t":"Goal 5.1 – Integrated planning and implementation"},{"t":"4.    Integrate ecological networks, ecological corridors, stepping stones and other measures that maintain, enhance or restore ecological connectivity into biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning, ecosystem restoration, climate change adaptation and relevant sectoral and infrastructure planning, in accordance with national circumstances, priorities and legislation."},{"t":"Goal 5.2 – Equitable governance and enabling conditions"},{"t":"5.     Promote equitable and effective governance, the full and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, the recognition and respect for their rights, including over their traditional territories, and the application of free, prior and informed consent,12 as applicable, while"},{"t":"12 “Free, prior and informed consent” refers to the tripartite terminology of “prior and informed consent”, “free, prior and"},{"t":"informed consent” and “approval and involvement”."},{"t":"12/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"**昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標**","html":"<p><strong>昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標</strong></p>","en":[1]},{"md":"| 目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **目標 22** | | |\n| 34. 加強原住民族與地方社區在與保護區及保育共生地相關之決策過程中的資訊取得，以及完整、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應性的代表性與參與，在適用情況下，應認可原住民族與傳統領地。 | | B |\n| 35. [確保][在可能情況下促進] 原住民族與地方社區、女性、兒童、青年及身心障礙者取得司法救濟，[並促進建立有效且易於使用的申訴機制，] 應符合國家立法及其他相關國際協議，以處理與[保護區及保育共生地之建立、管理與治理相關之議題，在適用情況下，應認可原住民族與傳統領地]。 | | |\n| 36. [確保][在可能情況下促進] 致力於與[保護區及保育共生地相關之活動，在適用情況下，應認可原住民族與傳統領地]之環境人權捍衛者獲得完整保護，[且應符合國家立法及相關國際文書與義務]。 | | |\n| **目標 23** | | |\n| 37. 促進性別平等，並根據國家立法，在工作計畫中整合具性別回應性的方法，包括使用[按性別分類之資料]及其他相關之分類指標，[並適當考慮性別暴力]。 | | A |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 22</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">34. 加強原住民族與地方社區在與保護區及保育共生地相關之決策過程中的資訊取得，以及完整、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應性的代表性與參與，在適用情況下，應認可原住民族與傳統領地。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">35. [確保][在可能情況下促進] 原住民族與地方社區、女性、兒童、青年及身心障礙者取得司法救濟，[並促進建立有效且易於使用的申訴機制，] 應符合國家立法及其他相關國際協議，以處理與[保護區及保育共生地之建立、管理與治理相關之議題，在適用情況下，應認可原住民族與傳統領地]。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">36. [確保][在可能情況下促進] 致力於與[保護區及保育共生地相關之活動，在適用情況下，應認可原住民族與傳統領地]之環境人權捍衛者獲得完整保護，[且應符合國家立法及相關國際文書與義務]。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>目標 23</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">37. 促進性別平等，並根據國家立法，在工作計畫中整合具性別回應性的方法，包括使用[按性別分類之資料]及其他相關之分類指標，[並適當考慮性別暴力]。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"**[II. 工作計畫要素 5：生態連結性**","html":"<p><strong>[II. 工作計畫要素 5：生態連結性</strong></p>","en":[7,8]},{"md":"**目標 3.**\n維持、增強並復育陸域、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系之結構性與功能性生態連結性，包括透過將具生態代表性且連結良好的[保護區及保育共生地系統，在適用情況下，應認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 整合至更廣泛的景觀與海景中。","html":"<p><strong>目標 3.</strong><br />\n維持、增強並復育陸域、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系之結構性與功能性生態連結性，包括透過將具生態代表性且連結良好的[保護區及保育共生地系統，在適用情況下，應認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 整合至更廣泛的景觀與海景中。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"**長期目標 5.1 – 整合規劃與執行**\n4.\n根據國家情況、優先事項及立法，將生態網絡、生態廊道、踏腳石及其他維持、增強或復育生態連結性的措施，整合至具生物多樣性包容性的空間規劃、生態系復育、氣候變遷調適以及相關部門與基礎設施規劃中。","html":"<p><strong>長期目標 5.1 – 整合規劃與執行</strong><br />\n4.<br />\n根據國家情況、優先事項及立法，將生態網絡、生態廊道、踏腳石及其他維持、增強或復育生態連結性的措施，整合至具生物多樣性包容性的空間規劃、生態系復育、氣候變遷調適以及相關部門與基礎設施規劃中。</p>","en":[10,11]},{"md":"**長期目標 5.2 – 公平治理與賦能條件**\n5.\n促進公平且有效的治理、原住民族與地方社區之完整且有效參與、對其權利（包括其傳統領地權利）之認可與尊重，以及在適用情況下，落實自由、事先及知情同意，¹²","html":"<p><strong>長期目標 5.2 – 公平治理與賦能條件</strong><br />\n5.<br />\n促進公平且有效的治理、原住民族與地方社區之完整且有效參與、對其權利（包括其傳統領地權利）之認可與尊重，以及在適用情況下，落實自由、事先及知情同意，¹²</p>","en":[12,13]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"¹²「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。","html":"<p>¹²「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。</p>","en":[14,15,16]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c-v-4/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae0473d58b9a83bc4d49172/p013.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – version 4 – 27 October 2026 – 3.20 p.m."},{"t":"strengthening financial resources, capacity-building and development, technical and scientific cooperation and access to and transfer of technology."},{"t":"Goal 5.3 – Cooperation and coordination"},{"t":"6.    Strengthen, as appropriate, national, transboundary and cross-sectoral cooperation on ecological connectivity and promote synergies with the Convention on the Conservation of Migratory Species of Wild Animals13 and other relevant multilateral environmental agreements and initiatives, in accordance with their respective mandates and while avoiding duplication."},{"t":"Goal 5.4 – Monitoring and knowledge"},{"t":"7.    Strengthen nationally appropriate approaches and indicators for monitoring structural and functional ecological connectivity, drawing on scientific information and indigenous and local knowledge, subject to free, prior and informed consent, as applicable, and taking into account relevant findings of the methodological assessment of integrated biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning and ecological connectivity of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services once approved by the Plenary of the Platform.]"},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"13 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1651, No. 28395."},{"t":"13/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"非正式文件（Non-paper）關於議程項目 17 (c) – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20","html":"<p>非正式文件（Non-paper）關於議程項目 17 (c) – 第 4 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日 – 下午 3:20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"強化財務資源、能力建構與發展、技術與科學合作，以及技術的取得與轉移。","html":"<p>強化財務資源、能力建構與發展、技術與科學合作，以及技術的取得與轉移。</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"長期目標 5.3 – 合作與協調","html":"<p>長期目標 5.3 – 合作與協調</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"6.\n視適當情況，強化關於生態連結性的國家、跨境及跨部門合作，並促進與《保護遷徙野生動物公約》$^{13}$及其他相關多邊環境協議與倡議之間的綜效，並應符合各自的職權且避免重複。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n視適當情況，強化關於生態連結性的國家、跨境及跨部門合作，並促進與《保護遷徙野生動物公約》<sup>13</sup>及其他相關多邊環境協議與倡議之間的綜效，並應符合各自的職權且避免重複。</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"長期目標 5.4 – 監測與知識","html":"<p>長期目標 5.4 – 監測與知識</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"7.\n強化用於監測結構性與功能性生態連結性的國家適當方法與指標，並利用科學資訊以及在符合自由、事先與知情同意（視適用情況而定）的前提下，利用原住民族與地方知識，並考量「生物多樣性與生態系服務之政府間科學－政策平台」對於整合生物多樣性友善空間規劃與生態連結性之方法論評估相關結果（一旦經該平台全體會議批准）。]","html":"<p>7.<br />\n強化用於監測結構性與功能性生態連結性的國家適當方法與指標，並利用科學資訊以及在符合自由、事先與知情同意（視適用情況而定）的前提下，利用原住民族與地方知識，並考量「生物多樣性與生態系服務之政府間科學－政策平台」對於整合生物多樣性友善空間規劃與生態連結性之方法論評估相關結果（一旦經該平台全體會議批准）。]</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"__________","html":"<hr />","en":[5]},{"md":"$^{13}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 1651 卷，第 28395 號。","html":"<p><sup>13</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1651 卷，第 28395 號。</p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"13/13","html":"<p>13/13</p>","en":[8]}]}]};
